---
description: Cloudflare Credentials Guardrials
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---


- use the cloudfared tunnel command with the --credentials-file argument to obtaining cloudflare credentials.  E.g. (bash cloudflared tunnel token --credentials-file /path/to/credentials.json tunnel-name)

- Avoid manually creating json files with tokens.  
- If you experience invalid credential errors, be wary about trying to manually create a json file, as this tends to produce errors that endlessly produce new errors during troubleshooting
- Always use --credentials-file for proper JSON format
- Check user context - ensure commands run as the right user
- Handle existing tunnels gracefully - don't assume they need to be created
- Test credentials automatically - don't assume they work
- Provide better user experience in ansible playbooks or scripts for troubleshooting cloudflare- clear guidance and pauses when needed